.nh
.TH "PB-DEVICE-AVAILABILITY" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-device-availability - Set device sleep availability


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb device availability <device> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set device sleep availability

.PP
Set whether the selected device remains available while idle or is allowed to sleep, according to --mode. Keep-awake mode requires a confirmation code because it can affect battery use and heat.

.PP
Devices are account enrollments with independent names, capabilities, and revocation state. Changes target the selected device, while pb setup configures the current machine. Revocation disconnects an enrollment rather than just hiding it from the list.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	six-character confirmation code for keep-awake mode

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for availability

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	availability mode: allow-sleep or keep-awake


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-device(1)\fP
